<title>FRANCE: Paris air cargo export traffic up 1.2pct in Q1.</title>
<headline>Paris air cargo export traffic up 1.2pct in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total of 138,816 tonnes of air cargo exports left the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in January-March 1997, up 1.2 percent on the same period last year, airport authority figures show.</p>
<p>January-March 1997 export traffic from the Paris  airports, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on January-March 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>Domestic	     10,370		 down 8.2 percent</p>
<p>European Union     17,316		  up 11.9</p>
<p>Non-EU Europe	 3,164		   up 6.8</p>
<p>North Africa	  2,382		down 11.1</p>
<p>Sub-Saharan Africa 11,278		   up 5.0</p>
<p>North America	38,211		   up 4.9</p>
<p>French territories  6,325		 down 7.2</p>
<p>Latin America	 7,693		   up 6.0</p>
<p>Middle East	  13,549		 down 0.6</p>
<p>Far East	     28,528		 down 4.5</p>
<p>    Total	   138,816		   up 1.2</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
</text>
